    sffi_torch_dynamic_facade_lexical_owner_gap_2026-08-27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-61127: reproduced RED (5/7 new-spec scenarios failing): src/lib/common/torch/dyn_sffi_ops.spl re-declared 12 raw externs locally - the legacy fixed-dim rt_torch_tensor_{zeros,ones,rand,randn,full,empty}(d0..ndim[,fill]) collided by name with the provider's array-form ([i64]) ABI (unbacked by ANY engine: C++ runtime and Rust runtime register only the array form), and rt_torch_torchtensor_eye/arange/linspace were name-variants with no runtime symbol at all; 61 raw calls sat in ad-hoc inline unsafe blocks (only 7 had private owners); interpreter vs native registrations diverged on scalar ops (C++ rt_torch_torchtensor_sub_scalar vs Rust rt_torch_sub_scalar). Fix: provider src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/torch/sffi.spl added the 3 missing backed externs (rt_torch_torchtensor_linalg_solve, _sub_scalar, _div_scalar) + exports (sole raw owner); dyn_sffi_ops.spl removed all 12 local declarations and routes every raw call through a private @always_inline fn _dyn_torch_*_raw owner (37 owners, 1 per ABI contract family); typed wrappers hold zero unsafe blocks; eye/arange/linspace switched to backed provider names rt_torch_tensor_*; the unowned legacy fixed-dim family (24 wrappers) fails closed (availability + dimension guards, then typed Err(unbacked_provider_abi) - never an unbacked FFI call); dyn_sffi.spl dropped the 12 raw-name re-exports; scripts/audit/torch-dyn-sffi-authority.shs now gates 0 extern fn in facade + owner-only unsafe + 37 owner calls + legacy fail-closed marker (PASS owner_raw_calls=37 local_extern_decls=0 wrapper_unsafe_blocks=0). Specs: new dyn_sffi_lexical_owner_spec 7/7 (was 2/7), dyn_sffi_ops_readiness 20/20 (2 stale scenarios updated), dyn_sffi_tensor_ops_status PASS; neighbours torch_scalar_out_slot_borrow, sffi_out_slot_callers_borrow, extended/torch_tensor_unit, app/llm_caret/local_torch, linalg_backend_probe_typed_error all PASS; census ratchet --summary PASS (14635 <= 19412). Residuals (pre-existing, other lanes): torch_device_placement_status 2, torch_training_seed_status 2, raw_memory_owner 4 fail identically at HEAD; census full mode hits a Git-Bash /dev/stdout awk quirk (pre-existing; --summary works); the Rust-C++ sub/div_scalar registration alignment remains an engine item (provider now documents the C++ contract family); sealed-complete admission unchanged (unsafe-only stands). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/lib/common/torch/dyn_sffi_lexical_owner_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/lib/common/torch/dyn_sffi_ops_readiness_spec.spl"

